#
# The projection-agreement gate (INHABITED-RUNTIME-STACK.md §Upper-projections,
# INHABITED-COMPETENCY.md §Performance): "the projection and the canon must
# agree" (Principle 7). The flat one-hop shortcuts gmeow:generatedForSubject /
# gmeow:generatedUnderConfiguration are COMPUTED projections of the multi-hop
# de-conflation path. This query returns, side by side, the shortcut's value AND
# the value obtained by walking the full nested canon
# (output → gmeow:wasGeneratedBy → invocation → gmeow:subEventOf → session →
# gmeow:sessionSubjectStage / gmeow:sessionConfiguration). The competency cell
# pins BOTH columns to the SAME IRI, so any disagreement between the flat shortcut
# and the collapse of the canon changes the row set and fails the gate — the
# executable proof that the commuting diagram commutes (flat = collapse(nested)).
# This is the STANDALONE terminus (the subject STAGE); the agent-runtime profile
# extends the collapse through gmeow:stageOfLineage to the durable lineage.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
SELECT ?shortcutSubject ?auditSubject ?shortcutConfig ?auditConfig WHERE {
    ?output gmeow:generatedForSubject ?shortcutSubject ;
        gmeow:generatedUnderConfiguration ?shortcutConfig ;
        gmeow:wasGeneratedBy ?invocation .
    ?invocation gmeow:subEventOf ?session .
    ?session gmeow:sessionSubjectStage ?auditSubject ;
        gmeow:sessionConfiguration ?auditConfig .
}
